WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.969
- Much respect as this
series comes to an end.

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.732
- A magnificent Game 7 performance,
sending home the Clippers.

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:07.518
- What a battle.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.770
- The Los Angeles Lakers
eliminate the Houston Rockets.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:11.899
- Frustration for the Bucks.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.870
- Question from Jonathan
down in the bubble.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:14.550
- TNT.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:15.220
- Right over here.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.189
- So much has happened in the NBA bubble.

00:00:19.828 --> 00:00:20.380
- Uh-oh.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.780
- Was that an ankle?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.119
- So as a journey comes to an end—

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.450
- A shocking upset.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.150
- The best team in the NBA is gone.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:29.504
- We're asking players to
give us their last word

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:33.070
on their NBA bubble experience.

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:36.910
So what are your last words
on this bubble experience?

00:00:37.318 --> 00:00:40.849
- [Laughing] Last word?

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.078
Um...

00:00:42.616 --> 00:00:45.520
- Um, last words would be...

00:00:46.748 --> 00:00:48.684
- That's tough for me right now.

00:00:48.857 --> 00:00:51.220
- I don't know what you want me to say,
but I just lost, so I don’t really

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.153
care what go on in the bubble now.

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.202
- I'm ready to go home.

00:00:58.075 --> 00:00:59.792
- Guess I get to see my
kids and my family.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.079
- Not really sure.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.205
Next question.

00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:07.957
- The bubble is a bubble.

00:01:07.957 --> 00:01:09.270
It was challenging.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.794
It was an experiment.

00:01:12.794 --> 00:01:13.600
An experience.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.729
- Ending on the loss,
disappointed, of course.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:19.339
But, you know, it's an
experience I'll never forget.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.089
- Our mission was to come down here
and be the last team standing.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.210
We fell short of that.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.791
- I think that whoever's crowned champion
deserve it cuz it's definitely the

00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:30.640
toughest time I've had in the NBA.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.620
- Obviously it didn't end how we wanted
it to, but, overall the experience.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.210
A lot of ups and downs, a lot
of craziness in this world.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.710
I'm just happy that the NBA,
you know, myself can give

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.310
something and for the world to
be excited about and proud about.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.889
♪♪♪ We celebrate the healing scars.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.059
Back to back like it's no tomorrow. ♪♪♪

00:01:47.059 --> 00:01:48.059
- I thought it was good.

00:01:48.059 --> 00:01:51.970
We didn't end up accomplishing what
we wanted to and what we needed.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.830
But I thought we had a lot of fun.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:01.930
- Pain that's on my face right now, the
way I feel, I can only imagine what’s

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.143
going through these victims’ families.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.260
- I think the job is getting done
as far as what we came here for.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.839
And I'm not talking about
finishing the season.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.529
I'm talking about coming
together as a brotherhood and

00:02:21.889 --> 00:02:23.190
getting our message across.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.420
- First time guys have ever worn
these messages on their jerseys

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.750
that I can, that I know of,
especially for this amount of time.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.529
And, you know, the main thing that
we were trying to do here was push

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.639
that message as well as play a game
that we love, that that’s our job.

00:02:39.389 --> 00:02:42.119
- There's a lot of injustice still
happening with the Black community.

00:02:42.119 --> 00:02:43.260
- Justice for Breonna Taylor.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.719
Justice for everybody—well, every
Black American out there that are being

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.790
harmed by police and police brutality.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.317
- I appreciate the NBA and everybody
listening for continuing to preach

00:02:55.317 --> 00:02:59.894
that message because it’s not stopping.

00:02:59.969 --> 00:03:01.150
- The job isn't done yet.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.650
And we can't stop until
Black lives really do matter.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:09.470
- I ain't gonna lie to you.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:14.880
A few months ago when they told
us about the bubble, none of us

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:15.770
were really excited about it.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.899
- We were all skeptical coming into it.

00:03:17.929 --> 00:03:21.350
Just, you know, it was unprecedented
times, not knowing what's gonna go on.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:28.309
- Obviously playing in a place like this
with no family, no fans, it was tough.

00:03:28.642 --> 00:03:33.647
- We’re happy with the way we have
had to keep the game of basketball

00:03:33.647 --> 00:03:37.070
going at the highest level and at
the same time, keep people safe.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.250
- The NBA did a good job of,
you know, hosting this event.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:44.410
- As a whole, I think they made it
really, they made it really fun for us.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.010
It’s a basketball paradise.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.820
- It was also very fun to compete
against so many peers, you know, in

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.500
this space, this AAU-like atmosphere.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.250
- It was way more than I expected.

00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:54.447
Super fun.

00:03:54.447 --> 00:03:57.629
Gave me a chance to bond with
my teammates and get closer and

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:00.006
get back to the game I love.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:03.329
- I just wanna say thank you to everybody
that prepared the food, that made

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.799
everything as comfortable as can be for
the players and everybody staying here.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:09.940
I really am grateful for your sacrifice.

00:04:10.139 --> 00:04:12.220
- I just wanna thank everyone that
was involved in this bubble.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.640
You guys made it, you know,
much easier for us to be here.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.610
- The NBA did an unbelievable job
keeping everything professional

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.420
and us protected, and we have to
continue to keep that momentum going.

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:26.590
- Our run is over and, you know, I'll
continue going back to doing my work.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:31.140
- We will use our platform and
able to not only compete on

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.510
the court, but be champions off
the court for our communities.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:39.530
- We used our platform for our voices
to be heard on the social injustices.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.499
- You know, we're still trying to send
a message and talk to the world, and

00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:44.109
we’re still gonna keep doing that.

00:04:44.109 --> 00:04:45.550
♪♪♪ Celebrate the progress,
that’s how we mobbin’ ♪♪♪

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.279
- To come together as a group and
try to figure out ways to continue

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.720
to impact society, I think
we've continued to do that and

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.480
hopefully we continue to uplift.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.890
- We made a difference in the
world with our short time here.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.320
And it's gonna continue to be a good
thing for for everybody in the league.

00:04:59.429 --> 00:05:03.789
- For me, I turn my focus back, you know,
to some of these problems that we have

00:05:03.799 --> 00:05:09.380
going on and being able to help out, you
know, help out in whatever ways I can.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:13.730
- Definitely one experience of a
lifetime, and it's something that

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:14.770
we never thought would happen.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.282
- It was a tough process, but, you
know, I was glad I was a part of it.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:18.499
You're all part of history.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:23.170
- I think overall it shows that basketball
will continue throughout any event.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.710
Basketball will always
bring people together.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.350
We can have a voice while playing
basketball, and I'll be there

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.543
in another bubble if it happens.

00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:36.870
- So I think that the bubble
was a success and, yeah, time

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.290
to leave this motherf--ker.

